1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,200
cos is how AI compares. You learned it for triangles.

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:05,600
AI turns everything it knows into arrows.

3
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:08,000
Two things. Two arrows.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,400
How alike they are IS the angle between them. And nobody can measure that angle.

5
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:13,600
Count them off the grid. a is 5 across and 0 up. b is 3 across and 4 up. That is all an arrow is.

6
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:18,400
Multiply the matching numbers and add. Five times three, plus zero times four. Fifteen. Drag it into the top.

7
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:22,400
Each arrow is 5 long. Five times five is twenty five.

8
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:25,600
Drag that into the bottom.

9
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:28,800
Fifteen divided by twenty five is nought point six.

10
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:31,200
That is the score for this angle — a number nobody measured.

11
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:32,800
One is the same direction. Zero is nothing in common. AI calls this cosine similarity.

12
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:36,400
We learned this at school. Nobody ever said what for.

13
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:40,000
Pause. Observe. Learn. Follow for the math behind AI — @observer.collapse
